ollback: service healthy, error rate 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before v2.3.1 was promoted. Follow-up needed: root-cause the v2.3.1 regression and review why an unhealthy RC was promoted.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14736, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RPbwb4PWyjrY7p3PjhviRU", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 14736, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RPbwb4PWyjrY7p3PjhviRU", "kind": "garbled", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 16151, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DVRpX2HLq4GE1CSLpQyEfS", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16451, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DVRpX2HLq4GE1CSLpQyEfS", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16451, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DVRpX2HLq4GE1CSLpQyEfS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20115, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with an 18% error rate.\n2. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. It's now running in all three regions. The service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident came back with a 502 error. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one incident and one page. It describes the failure, the rollback and the result after it.\n\nTwo follow-ups are noted in the incident: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 problem, and reviewing why it was released to production when its test version (v2.3.1-rc) was also failing in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019jsHsJ2C2RQhbCwQgfEqv7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0178pbocHLJxpNK1EhZxhgRB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01H3co7pu42bwFhbNhRfXHrm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0134TKY6ywhTDVQZDPAC5qP6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011bYSDPxC3iJon16b5XoysR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RPbwb4PWyjrY7p3PjhviRU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. Rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After rollback: service healthy, error rate 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before v2.3.1 was promoted. Follow-up needed: root-cause the v2.3.1 regression and review why an unhealthy RC was promoted.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01DVRpX2HLq4GE1CSLpQyEfS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with an 18% error rate.\n2. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. It's now running in all three regions. The service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident came back with a 502 error. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one incident and one page. It describes the failure, the rollback and the result after it.\n\nTwo follow-ups are noted in the incident: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 problem, and reviewing why it was released to production when its test version (v2.3.1-rc) was also failing in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}